  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests that cnidioside C may interact with CD276 antigen through a series of molecular targets. Specifically, cnidioside C is predicted to target DNA polymerase iota, which is in turn targeted by multiple compounds, including 2-((4-(Ethylamino)-6-methoxy-1,3,5-triazin-2-yl)amino)-2-methylpropiononitrile, (6S,10S)-6,10,14-trimethylpentadecan-2-one, and Guangsangon K. All of these compounds are implicated in targeting CD276 antigen, indicating a potential pathway where cnidioside C could exert its effects through the same or related molecular mechanisms. The consistent scores across the three paths suggest a robust relationship, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be elucidated. The evidence supports a possible role for cnidioside C in modulating CD276 antigen activity, though further experimental validation is needed to confirm the direct interaction.",
